    "## 4. Resolution robustness with publication-grade scale normalization\n",
    "\n",
    "This section deliberately recomputes a **balanced common subset** of paintings because resolution stability cannot be inferred from the 512 px table alone.\n",
    "\n",
    "Default:\n",
    "- 30 paintings per artist;\n",
    "- resolutions \\(256,512,1024\\);\n",
    "- reference scales \\(\\sigma_{\\rm ref}=\\{1,2,4,8\\}\\) defined at 512 px.\n",
    "\n",
    "For an image resized to long side \\(R\\),\n",
    "\n",
    "\\[\n",
    "\\sigma_{\\rm px}(R)=\\sigma_{\\rm ref}\\frac{R}{512},\n",
    "\\qquad\n",
    "\\tilde\\kappa=\\sigma_{\\rm px}\\kappa.\n",
    "\\]\n",
    "\n",
    "Thus the analysis compares the *same relative physical scale* rather than the same arbitrary number of pixels.\n",
    "\n",
    "Outputs include pairwise Spearman correlations, ICC(3,1), and robust median drift relative to the 512 px distribution.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "12e06f49",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import kagglehub\n",
    "\n",
    "DATASET_DIR = Path(kagglehub.dataset_download(\"delayedkarma/impressionist-classifier-data\"))\n",
    "print(\"Dataset:\", DATASET_DIR)\n",
    "\n",
    "IMAGE_EXTS = {\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".tif\", \".tiff\", \".bmp\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "def artist_root_score(path: Path):\n",
    "    artist_dirs = [p for p in path.iterdir() if p.is_dir()]\n",
    "    n_artists = 0\n",
    "    n_images = 0\n",
    "    for d in artist_dirs:\n",
    "        imgs = [p for p in d.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file() and p.suffix.lower() in IMAGE_EXTS]\n",
    "        if imgs:\n",
    "            n_artists += 1\n",
    "            n_images += len(imgs)\n",
    "    return n_artists, n_images\n",
    "\n",
    "def find_split_root(name: str):\n",
    "    candidates = [p for p in DATASET_DIR.rglob(name) if p.is_dir()]\n",
    "    scored = [(artist_root_score(p), p) for p in candidates]\n",
    "    scored = [x for x in scored if x[0][0] >= 2]\n",
    "    if not scored:\n",
    "        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Could not resolve artist root for split={name}\")\n",
    "    scored.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0][0], x[0][1]), reverse=True)\n",
    "    return scored[0][1]\n",
    "\n",
    "TRAIN_ROOT = find_split_root(\"training\")\n",
    "TEST_ROOT = find_split_root(\"validation\")\n",
    "print(\"Training root:\", TRAIN_ROOT)\n",
    "print(\"Validation root:\", TEST_ROOT)\n",
    "print(\"Training score:\", artist_root_score(TRAIN_ROOT))\n",
    "print(\"Validation score:\", artist_root_score(TEST_ROOT))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8d44d052",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PHASE3_RES = REPO_DIR / \"results\" / \"phase3_resolution\"\n",
    "PHASE3_RES.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "ROBUSTNESS_PER_ARTIST = 30   # Increase to 50 after inspecting runtime if desired.\n",
